O|            F A R G O #401 Blue Rev. - 11/18/19 2A.   
O|
N,G|               We see MEN in hats on the street outside the club. This is           
N|               THE MOSKOWITZ CONTINGENCY. They control gambling,                    
N|               prostitution, etc.                                                   
O|
O|            No portion of this script may be performed, published, reproduced, sold or distributed by any means or quoted or published
O|       in any medium, without prior written consent of FX Productions, LLC. In no event, may any participant monetize or profit off the script in any way.
O|                              © 2018 FX Productions, LLC. All rights reserved.      
O|            F A R G O #401 WHITE PRODUCTION DRAFT - 11/18/19 3.
O|
S|       4       INT. JACKSON DEMOCRATIC CLUB. KANSAS CITY - DAY                4     
N|               Inside the club, local Missourians indulge their baser               
N,G|               instincts. Cards are played. Prostitutes visible in the              
N,G|               background. Around them we see Jewish gangsters at work,             
N|               keeping things orderly.                                              
O|
N,G,I|               We PUSH INTO a CLOSE UP of Jewish Boss, LIEV MOSKOWITZ (50s) -       
N,I|               - a concrete slab of a man with a face straight out of               
N|               Deuteronomy.                                                         
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         Then came the Irish.                                       
T|                                                                CUT TO:             
O|
S|       5       EXT. JACKSON DEMOCRATIC CLUB. KANSAS CITY, MO - DAY            5     
O|
N,G|               Same angle, same street.                                             
O|
N|               The Year 1920 --                                                     
O|
N|               The clothes have changed, but it’s still very much an                
N|               immigrant community -- the neighborhood now less Jewish, more        
N|               Irish.                                                               
N,G|               As we watch, TWO GROUPS OF MEN approach each other: The              
N|               Moskowitz Contingency and a group of Irish immigrants we will        
N|               call THE MILLIGAN SYNDICATE. The two groups appraise each            
N|               other warily.                                                        
O|
N,I|               Liev SPITS INTO HIS HAND, offers it to OWNEY “YIDDLES”               
N,I|               MILLIGAN (40s), a wily Irishman with a facial scar.                  
O|
N|               Yiddles spits in his own hand. They shake.                           
O|
T|                                                                CUT TO:             
O|
S|       6       INT. JACKSON DEMOCRATIC CLUB. KANSAS CITY - DAY (1920)         6     
O|
N|               Later. The two gangs are gathered in the big room, tables            
N|               pushed back towards the wall, a center circle open -- Jews on        
N|               one side, Irish on the other.                                        
O|
N,I|               A young Jewish boy stands next to his father. This is Liev’s         
N,I|               youngest son, ARI MOSKOWITZ, 11.                                     
O|
N,G|               As we watch, the boss gives Ari a push toward the center of          
N|               the room. Ari walks out into the open.                               
O|
O|            No portion of this script may be performed, published, reproduced, sold or distributed by any means or quoted or published
O|       in any medium, without prior written consent of FX Productions, LLC. In no event, may any participant monetize or profit off the script in any way.
O|                              © 2018 FX Productions, LLC. All rights reserved.      
O|            F A R G O #401 Green Rev. - 11/18/19 4.   
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         To keep the peace, the boss of each                        
U|                         family gave offer of his youngest                          
U|                         son in trade.                                              
G|               ANGLE ON YIDDLES                                                     
O|
N,I|               who pushes his own son, PATRICK, 7, out to meet Ari. Patrick         
N|               wears A CAP that’s too large for him.                                
O|
N|               We’re not clear. Are they supposed to fight?                         
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         The thinkin’ was -- by raisin’ your                        
U|                         enemy’s offspring an understandin’                         
U|                         could be reached, and peace                                
U|                         maintained.                                                
G|               ANGLE ON BOSS MOSKOWITZ                                              
O|
N|               who beckons the Irish lad over. Patrick approaches                   
N|               reluctantly. Moskowitz pinches his cheek.                            
O|
C|                                   MOSKOWITZ                                        
U|                         Relax, boychick.                                           
P|                             (in Yiddish)                                           
U|                         Bist shoyn eyner fun undz.                                 
N|               You’re one of us now.                                                
O|
G|               ANGLE ON YIDDLES                                                     
O|
N|               The scar on his face is old, the memory of a fight from his          
N|               youth barely won. These days though he wins them all -- one          
N|               way or another.                                                      
O|
N|               Yiddles pulls out a flask, drinks, then offers the flask to          
N|               11-year-old Ari.                                                     
O|
C|                                   YIDDLES                                          
U|                         Put some hair on yer bollocks.                             
N|               The boy drinks. Everybody cheers.                                    
O|
G|               ANGLE ON LIEV MOSKOWITZ                                              
O|
N|               With murder in his eyes, he watches this scarred gentile             
N|               corrupt his son.                                                     
O|
T|                                                                CUT TO:             
O|
