O|                              © 2018 FX Productions, LLC. All rights reserved.      
O|            F A R G O #401 Pink Rev. - 11/18/19 5.     
O|
S|       7       INT. PRINCIPAL’S OFFICE. HIGH SCHOOL - DAY                     7     
N|               Again, Ethelrida is pushed in front of the cinder block wall.        
N|               She is in a new outfit, sporting a raw left eye. She’s been          
N|               punched.                                                             
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         See, the problem wasn’t that I was                         
U|                         disreputable.                                              
O|
G|               ANGLE ON MS. HAGBLOOM                                                
O|
N|               Same sour expression.                                                
C|                                   MS. HAGBLOOM                                     
U|                         What’d you do this time?                                   
O|
C|                                   ETHELRIDA                                        
U|                         Punched Dolores Disfarmer with my                          
U|                         eye, a course.                                             
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         I was, in fact, a student of                               
U|                         exceptional virtue and high                                
U|                         achievement.                                               
O|
G|               ANGLE ON PRINCIPAL CRISCOE                                           
N|               He steps into the doorway, paddle in hand and glares at              
N|               Ethelrida.                                                           
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         The problem was -- the only thing                          
U|                         worse than a disreputable negro,                           
U|                         was an upstanding one.                                     
O|
T|                                                                CUT TO:             
O|
S|       8       INT. HALLWAY. GROVER CLEVELAND HIGH SCHOOL. KANSAS CITY, MO -  8     
S|               DAY (1950)                                                           
N,G|               Ms. HAGBLOOM walks ETHELRIDA down the hall. We see a JANITOR         
N|               wiping graffiti from the wall.                                       
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         And so I endured the slings and                            
U|                         arrows of small minded folk who, in                        
U|                         their narrow thoughts, imagined                            
U|                         they could teach me a lesson.                              
O|
T|                                                                CUT TO:             
