O|            F A R G O #401 WHITE PRODUCTION DRAFT - 11/18/19 7.
O|
G|               ANGLE ON PATRICK                                                     
N|               still just a child. The boy on the floor cries, looking up at        
N|               him. But there is no room for childhood here. Patrick knows          
N|               what he has to do. But he can’t.                                     
O|
N|               YIDDLES                                                              
O|
N|               sees his weakness. He GRABS his son’s gun hand, aims at Ari.         
O|
C,E|                                   YIDDLES (CONT'D)                                 
U|                         Chew him up.                                               
O|
N|               He squeezes his son’s hand, hurting him.                             
G|               ANGLE ON THE TRIGGER                                                 
O|
N|               As Yiddles forces Patrick to pull it.                                
O|
N|               -- BANG --                                                           
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         Logic dictates that in every fight                         
U|                         there is a winner and a loser.                             
O|
G|               AN OVERHEAD ANGLE                                                    
N|               of the massacre. As the Irish search the bodies of their             
N|               enemies for valuables.                                               
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         But this is a history report, and                          
U|                         what does history tell us?                                 
O|
T|                                                                CUT TO:             
O|
S|       10      EXT. JACKSON DEMOCRATIC CLUB. KANSAS CITY - DAY (1928)        10     
O|
N,G|               Same angle, same street.                                             
N|               The Year 1928.                                                       
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         Peace don’t last for long.                                 
O|
N,G|               Yiddles Milligan and his gang enter frame left, cocky with           
N|               power. Now they’re the establishment, and as far as they’re          
N|               concerned they’ll be kings forever.                                  
O|
N,I|               They are met by a group of ITALIAN MEN, led by DONATELLO             
N,I|               FADDA, 40s, head of the FADDA FAMILY.                                
O|
O|            No portion of this script may be performed, published, reproduced, sold or distributed by any means or quoted or published
O|       in any medium, without prior written consent of FX Productions, LLC. In no event, may any participant monetize or profit off the script in any way.
