O|            F A R G O #401 WHITE PRODUCTION DRAFT - 11/18/19 8.
O|
C,E|                                   ETHELRIDA (V.O.)                                 
U|                         The Italians came next. That’s how                         
U|                         it worked. Whoever was last off the                        
U|                         boat -- finding the doors of honest                        
U|                         capital closed -- rolled up their                          
U|                         sleeves and got to work gettin’                            
U|                         rich the old fashioned way.                                
G|               CLOSE UP ON DONATELLO                                                
O|
N|               A first generation immigrant from Sardinia, Donatello made           
N|               enough money killing anarchists for the Italian government to        
N|               smuggle himself over to the U.S. when he was seventeen.              
N,I|               Left behind was his beloved CHIANNA, who joined him six years        
N,I|               later with their son JOSTO, leaving their other son --               
N|               GATEANO in Italy.                                                    
O|
N|               Donatello is lean, lethal. He has known hunger so bad he once        
N|               ate the plaster from the walls, once ate the laces from his          
N|               shoes. He has come to America to slay all the fattened calfs,        
N|               to gorge on their flesh and banish hunger from his world.            
O|
G|               ANGLE ON YIDDLES                                                     
O|
N|               The Irish King of Kansas City, our disfigured, snake-                
N|               charming, back-stabber. He SPITS into his hand, offers it to         
N|               Donatello -- who SPITS in his own hand and shakes.                   
T|                                                                CUT TO:             
O|
S|       11      INT. JACKSON DEMOCRATIC CLUB. KANSAS CITY - DAY               11     
O|
N|               As before, the tables have been pushed back, a circle open in        
N|               the center of the room. The two gangs assemble across from           
N|               each other.                                                          
O|
N,I|               Donatello PUSHES FORWARD his son, JOSTO, 15. A handsome boy,         
N|               confident, ready to do his part for the family.                      
G|               ANGLE ON YIDDLES                                                     
O|
N,I|               He has a new son, MICHAEL, 8, on his left. Yiddles reaches           
N|               for him, then lowers his hand.                                       
O|
N,I|               With his right hand he PUSHES 15-year-old PATRICK towards the        
N|               Italians.                                                            
O|
G|               ANGLE ON PATRICK                                                     
O|
