N,G|               A GROUP of FADDA’S MEN enter frame left, walking in slow             
N|               motion.                                                              
N,G,I|               From frame right, walking to meet them, we see a SINGLE MAN --       
O|
N,I|               LOY CANNON, early 50s.                                               
O|
N|               Loy is a Being of Pure Self -- self-educated, self-made -- a         
N|               sophisticate born into an age of brutality. Raised in Harlem,        
N|               he was a child prodigy nobody nurtured. So -- fuck ‘em -- he         
N|               became a titan all by himself, moving west at fifteen to             
N|               escape the Dutch Shultz takeover of New York.                        
O|
N|               In a perfect world Loy would be CEO of a fortune 500 company.        
N|               But his world isn’t perfect. There are more doors closed to          
N|               him than open. So he created an empire of a different kind;          
N|               running numbers, prostitution, protection.                           
N|               But where white politicians and police look at Loy and see a         
N|               criminal, the black community sees Cannon Savings and Loan:          
N|               the only bank that will lend to them. They see Cannon                
N|               Fidelity Mutual: the only insurance company that will write          
N|               them a life insurance policy or give them home owner’s               
N|               insurance.                                                           
O|
N|               Welcome to the Alternate Economy.                                    
G|               ANGLE ON DONATELLO FADDA                                             
O|
N|               (now in his 60s) as he steps forward to meet Loy Cannon. The         
N|               two men study each other.                                            
O|
