O|
N|               A BUS pulls in. The doors open.                                      
O|
G|               CLOSE UP ON ETHELRIDA                                                
O|
N|               looking to see who will get off.                                     
O|
G|               ANGLE ON THE BUS                                                     
O|
N|               For a beat the OPEN DOORS create a dark hole. And then               
N|               Oraetta Mayflower steps down. She has a scarf tied around her        
N|               head, and, as the bus pulls away, she adjusts it in the wind.        
N|               She appears to be talking quietly to herself, but we don’t           
N|               hear her words.                                                      
N|               Watching her --                                                      
O|
N|               ETHELRIDA                                                            
O|
N|               has the sudden instinct to get out of sight. She ducks back          
N|               into the shadows.                                                    
O|
N|               As she watches, Oraetta crosses the street and approaches an         
N|               apartment building. She digs around for her keys, goes               
N|               inside.                                                              
O|
