G|               ANGLE ON ETHELRIDA                                                   
N|               She’s not sure why she’s watching, but something about this          
N|               neighbor just feels wrong.                                           
O|
G|               ANGLE ON THE APARTMENT BUILDING                                      
O|
N,G|               As a SECOND FLOOR LIGHT goes on. We see Oraetta inside her           
N|               apartment, taking off her coat.                                      
O|
G|               CLOSE UP ON ETHELRIDA                                                
O|
N|               She studies the window, then THURMAN comes to the door.              
C|                                   THURMAN                                          
U|                         Hon? Is that you?                                          
O|
N|               He steps out onto the porch, clutching his bathrobe against          
N|               the cold.                                                            
O|
C,E|                                   THURMAN (CONT'D)                                 
U|                         Jeez -- it’s freezin out here. Why                         
U|                         dontcha come inside?                                       
O|
C|                                   ETHELRIDA                                        
U|                         What’s gonna happen to me, dad? In                         
U|                         the world.                                                 
C|                                   THURMAN                                          
U|                         Oh, hon. It’s gonna be okay.                               
U|                         There’s a place fer all of us on                           
U|                         this Earth. We just have to find                           
U|                         it. Now come on in.                                        
O|
N|               Ethelrida stands, goes to the door.                                  
O|
C|                                   ETHELRIDA                                        
U|                         Who were those guys? In the                                
U|                         kitchen.                                                   
C|                                   THURMAN                                          
U|                         Well -- we’re just havin some money                        
U|                         trouble right now, yer mom and me.                         
U|                         Not a lot. And please don’t tell                           
U|                         her I said. She a very proud woman.                        
O|
C|                                   ETHELRIDA                                        
U|                         Are we gonna lose the house?                               
O|
N|               He hugs her.                                                         
O|
