C|                                   THURMAN                                          
U|                         No. Nothin’ like that. Just a bad                          
U|                         city inspection. Some renovations                          
U|                         to do. But we got it covered.                              
N|               Thurman pats her head.                                               
O|
C,E|                                   THURMAN (CONT'D)                                 
U|                         Want me to read to you? Help ya                            
U|                         fall back asleep.                                          
O|
C|                                   ETHELRIDA                                        
U|                         Dad, I’m sixteen.                                          
C|                                   THURMAN                                          
U|                         Doesn’t mean you don’t need a                              
U|                         bedtime story from time to time.                           
U|                         Whatdya say? Wizard of Oz?                                 
O|
N|               Ethelrida nods. That would be nice.                                  
O|
N|               She goes inside. Thurman follows. The front door closes.             
N|               Beat. The hall light turns off.                                      
O|
N,G|               Then the CAMERA PANS away, back to the street and PUSHES             
N,G|               TOWARDS the Apartment Building. We cross the street, focused         
N,G|               on the first floor, then start to RISE --                            
N,G|               And as we reach the second story we see Oraetta Mayflower at         
N|               her window, looking out. We get the feeling she has seen             
N|               everything from the moment she stepped off the bus.                  
O|
G|               We PUSH INTO A CLOSE UP                                              
O|
N|               Oraetta’s lips are moving, but we can’t hear what she says.          
O|
M|                                    END OF EPISODE 401                              
